              "text": "**Ukraine** (often spelled *Ucrania* in Spanish or Portuguese, and sometimes typed as *Ukrania*) is a country located in Eastern Europe. \n\nBecause your query was open-ended, here is a general overview of the country and its current status as of **May 2026**:\n\n### 1. General Overview\n* **Capital:** Kyiv\n* **Official Language:** Ukrainian\n* **Location:** It is the second-largest country by area in Europe, bordered by Russia to the east and northeast, Belarus to the north, Poland, Slovakia, and Hungary to the west, and Romania and Moldova to the southwest, with a coastline along the Black Sea and the Sea of Azov.\n\n### 2. Current Situation (May 2026)\nSince February 2022, Ukraine has been defending its sovereignty against a full-scale invasion by the Russian Federation. \n* **The Frontlines:** Over four years into the conflict, the war of attrition continues. While Russia continues heavy bombardment and localized grinding offensives (such as in the eastern and southern sectors like Kostyantynivka and Zaporizhzhia), the frontline has largely stabilized. \n* **The Drone War & Deep Strikes:** A defining feature of the conflict in 2026 is Ukraine\u2019s highly developed domestic drone program. Ukraine has frequently launched long-range drone strikes hitting military and economic infrastructure\u2014such as oil refineries and pumping stations deep inside Russian territory (including Saratov and Kirov)\u2014to disrupt Russia\u2019s military logistics.\n* **Air Defenses:** Ukraine continues to face significant aerial threats, with Russia launching massive missile and drone strikes targeting Kyiv and energy infrastructure. Ukraine remains highly reliant on Western military support, specifically seeking air defense systems like Patriot missiles to protect its skies.\n\n***\n\n**How can I help you further?** \n* Would you like the latest news and military updates on the conflict?\n* Are you looking for information on Ukrainian history, culture, or geography?\n* Do you need assistance in Spanish (*\u00bfPrefieres que te responda en espa\u00f1ol?*) or another language?",
